---
description: Keep app/ limited to routes and route-specific UI
globs: app/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# app/ — routes only

Allowed files: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `route.ts`, and UI used on that route only.

- Group routes: `app/(auth)/`, `app/(dashboard)/`, `app/(marketing)/`
- If a component is used on more than one route, move it to `components/`
- Pages fetch via `data/` in Server Components — never call Supabase here
- Mutations go through `actions/`, not inline in pages
- Every data-fetching route gets a colocated `loading.tsx` that renders shadcn `Skeleton`s. Next shows it automatically while the Server Component loads. Do not fake this with `useState` + Skeleton on first paint.

```
app/
├── (auth)/login/page.tsx
├── (dashboard)/projects/
│   ├── page.tsx
│   └── loading.tsx   ← Skeleton UI for this route
└── api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts
```

Top-of-screen progress on route changes is `NextTopLoader` in `app/layout.tsx`, not a per-route component.
